The GEOMETRY directive is really meant for placing things inside
maze areas (like the castle, asmo, etc), which is why it tries hard
to align on odd coordinates and thinks that the upper left corner
is (3,3) instead of (1,0). Making left geometry snap to column 1
wouldn't break anything but would violate this design. If you
change H_LEFT, CENTER, and H_RIGHT to give more accurate
results as well then things might start to break.

To fix the ranger level, you could put a MAP on the right side to obviate
the INIT_MAP and the ROOM fill character. You still wind up with
some foliage in column 79 that you can't do anything about, but
barring absolute geometry or 79-column MAPs, you can spruce things
up to look like you know what you're doing:

MAZE: "Ran-strt",' '
FLAGS: noteleport,hardfloor,arboreal
GEOMETRY:right,center
MAP
